tg-bridge — NOTICE

This is an independent implementation. No source files were copied from other
projects. Since v2.0 (current: v3) it is built on these open-source libraries (installed
from PyPI, pinned with hashes in requirements.txt, not vendored):

* aiogram 3.33.0 — MIT — https://github.com/aiogram/aiogram (Telegram Bot API client)
* aiohttp — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp (HTTP, via aiogram)
* tenacity 9.2.1 — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/jd/tenacity (retries)
* supervisor 4.3.0 — BSD-derived (repoze) — https://github.com/Supervisor/supervisor
  (process supervision, event listener protocol)
* Pillow — MIT-CMU — optional PNG->JPEG conversion for set-photo

The design was informed by reading the following open-source projects:

* deluminor/telegram-routine-bridge — MIT License, Copyright 2026 Erik Kopcha
  https://github.com/deluminor/telegram-routine-bridge
  Ideas used: strict owner allowlist (private chat only, from.id == chat.id,
  fail closed), secrets only from env/private file and never on the command line.

* jexmarc/grokbot-telegram — MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 grokbot-telegram contributors
  https://github.com/jexmarc/grokbot-telegram
  Ideas used: sendMessageDraft streaming, receipt reactions, marking Telegram
  content as untrusted in the routine payload.

Concepts only (these repositories had no license at the time of review, so no
code, text or structure was copied, only general ideas were re-implemented):

* clsasa1/grokbot-telegram-bridge — media/voice download, a tg-* CLI for replies.
* arismarioneves/grokbot-telegram — general relay-to-routine approach.

Telegram Bot API reference: https://core.telegram.org/bots/api (target: Bot API 10.5)

v4: inbound intake runs on Telegram Serverless (https://core.telegram.org/bots/serverless),
deployed and operated with Telegram's official CLI @tgcloud/cli (npm), pinned in
serverless/package-lock.json.

v4.1: outbound replies use Telegram Rich Messages (Bot API 10.1+) via aiogram 3.33 send_rich_message / send_rich_message_draft. Markdown is sent to the official API as-is; no third-party converter is vendored.
